1
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,906
<i>They say there's power in Boston.</i>

2
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:56,867
<i>Some phone service in Denver.</i>

3
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:02,290
<i>But things are far from what they were.</i>

4
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,381
<i>Maybe it was all inevitable.</i>

5
00:02:12,258 --> 00:02:15,720
<i>An unavoidable collision between
mankind and technology.</i>

6
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:27,982
<i>The Internet was meant to make
the world a smaller place.</i>

7
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:34,155
<i>But it actually feels smaller without it.</i>

8
00:02:44,165 --> 00:02:47,626
<i>I knew Will and Evelyn Caster
better than anyone.</i>

9
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,048
<i>I knew their brilliance.</i>

10
00:02:53,924 --> 00:02:57,011
<i>Their dedication to what they believed in.</i>

11
00:02:59,388 --> 00:03:01,557
<i>And to what they loved.</i>

12
00:03:14,195 --> 00:03:17,907
<i>The time has come for us to pause</i>

13
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:23,371
<i>And think of living as it was</i>

14
00:03:25,414 --> 00:03:31,587
<i>Into the future we must cross
Must cross</i>

15
00:03:32,421 --> 00:03:35,091
I'm not sure what the point is.

16
00:03:37,426 --> 00:03:40,179
Copper shields the electromagnetic radiation.

17
00:03:40,388 --> 00:03:45,184
Yeah, I know how it works.
I'm asking "Why?"

18
00:03:45,351 --> 00:03:46,727
Sanctuary.

19
00:03:46,894 --> 00:03:51,565
Nothing gets through.
No signals of any kind.

20
00:03:52,525 --> 00:03:55,361
- You see? Dead zone. Nothing.
- Uh-huh.

21
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:57,530
Sure, but you could just turn it off.

22
00:03:58,322 --> 00:04:01,784
Yeah, but fewer distractions is
what you wanted, right? Isn't it?

23
00:04:03,244 --> 00:04:05,913
Yeah. That's what I wanted.

24
00:04:06,956 --> 00:04:08,582
- Come on. We'll be late.
- For what?

25
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:24,849
- Hey, you know what?
- What?

26
00:04:25,015 --> 00:04:27,977
I really think I'm starting
to make progress on this.

27
00:04:28,144 --> 00:04:31,480
Hey. You need to get dressed.

28
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:40,197
I don't know why you
bother with these proofs.

29
00:04:40,364 --> 00:04:42,491
Only three people in the world even care.

30
00:04:42,658 --> 00:04:44,827
Because it's fun.

31
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:47,913
- You sure you're up for this?
- No. Not remotely.

32
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:51,000
Really? Will, it's important.

33
00:04:51,167 --> 00:04:53,377
I know, but your donors are fools.

34
00:04:53,544 --> 00:04:57,298
They sit there in a daze, waiting for me
to say "commercial application."

35
00:04:57,465 --> 00:04:58,757
It kills me.

36
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:03,971
Well, the "fools" there today could
fund us for the next five years.

37
00:05:04,138 --> 00:05:07,516
- In that case I have every reason to behave.
- Yes.

38
00:05:07,683 --> 00:05:12,062
But if this goes well, promise me that
I'll never have to do this ever again.

39
00:05:12,229 --> 00:05:14,273
- Never. Promise.
- Okay, I promise.

40
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,525
- Really?
- Sure, I promise.

41
00:05:17,902 --> 00:05:20,404
Ha, ha. You're lying.

42
00:05:54,939 --> 00:05:58,484
<i>Happy birthday, dear Erin</i>

43
00:05:58,943 --> 00:06:01,195
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

44
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:21,048
Jason. Other side of the stage.

45
00:06:21,215 --> 00:06:23,759
You'll do a camera and sound check together.

46
00:06:23,926 --> 00:06:26,512
You'll do the first block,
followed by McRae, Llewellyn.

47
00:06:26,679 --> 00:06:29,139
- And, ah, then the main event.
- Max.

48
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:31,934
- Ev, how are you?
- Good.

49
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:35,896
- Ready to sing for your supper?
- I'm sorry to put you through it.

50
00:06:36,105 --> 00:06:38,107
Dr. Caster? Sorry. Would you mind?

51
00:06:38,315 --> 00:06:39,817
Sure thing.

52
00:06:41,527 --> 00:06:42,736
Thanks.

53
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:44,905
You have groupies?
Why don't I get groupies?

54
00:06:45,072 --> 00:06:47,032
Dr. Waters, would you like a run-through?

55
00:06:47,199 --> 00:06:49,201
- Yes. I'll see you backstage.
- All right.

56
00:06:59,461 --> 00:07:01,630
<i>...important distinction.</i>

57
00:07:01,797 --> 00:07:05,759
<i>This created brain is self-sustaining.</i>

58
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:10,347
<i>And it's capable of emotional expressivity...</i>

59
00:07:10,514 --> 00:07:13,392
<i>...and of self-awareness.</i>

60
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:19,315
The effort to develop a strong
artificial intelligence...

61
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:23,277
...has led to significant advancements
in the field of neural engineering...

62
00:07:23,444 --> 00:07:26,238
...as well as our understanding
of the human brain.

63
00:07:26,405 --> 00:07:31,285
But while some focus on the still-distant
dream of a thinking computer...

64
00:07:31,452 --> 00:07:34,413
...I believe the journey...

65
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:37,166
...to be more important than the destination.

66
00:07:37,333 --> 00:07:41,420
My priority is to use my colleagues'
accidental insights...

67
00:07:41,587 --> 00:07:44,423
...to develop new methods
for the early detection of cancer...

68
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:47,635
...and in the hopes of finding
a cure for Alzheimer's.

69
00:07:48,135 --> 00:07:49,928
Simply put, to save lives.

70
00:08:10,199 --> 00:08:12,826
"A new type of thinking is essential...

71
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:16,455
...if mankind is to survive and
move toward higher levels."

72
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:20,542
Albert Einstein said that
more than 50 years ago.

73
00:08:20,709 --> 00:08:23,879
And it couldn't be more
relevant than it is today.

74
00:08:24,421 --> 00:08:26,590
Intelligent machines will soon allow us...

75
00:08:26,757 --> 00:08:30,010
...to conquer our most intractable challenges.

76
00:08:30,177 --> 00:08:34,515
Not merely to cure disease,
but to end poverty and hunger.

77
00:08:34,682 --> 00:08:36,308
To heal the planet.

78
00:08:36,475 --> 00:08:39,395
And build a better future for all of us.

79
00:08:39,561 --> 00:08:43,065
I don't know anybody who is doing
more to make that future a reality...

80
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:46,443
...than our next speaker.
But then again, I'm probably biased.

81
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:52,366
Please welcome my partner
in science and in life...

82
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:54,535
...Dr. Will Caster.

83
00:09:00,958 --> 00:09:02,835
Thank you very much.

84
00:09:03,502 --> 00:09:06,880
My wife has always been eager
to change the world.

85
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:09,758
But I'll just settle for understanding it first.

86
00:09:11,719 --> 00:09:15,055
For 130,000 years...

87
00:09:15,222 --> 00:09:19,435
...our capacity for reason
has remained unchanged.

88
00:09:19,977 --> 00:09:26,024
The combined intellect of the neuroscientists,
engineers, mathematicians and...

89
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:28,068
...hackers...

90
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:30,654
...in this auditorium...

91
00:09:30,821 --> 00:09:35,617
...pales in comparison
to even the most basic Al.

92
00:09:35,784 --> 00:09:41,165
Once online, a sentient machine will quickly
overcome the limits of biology.

93
00:09:41,331 --> 00:09:44,918
And in a short time,
its analytical power will be greater...

94
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:47,671
...than the collective intelligence...

95
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:52,676
...of every person born
in the history of the world.

96
00:10:05,189 --> 00:10:07,941
So now imagine such an entity...

97
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:11,737
...with a full range of human emotion.
Even self-awareness.

98
00:10:13,155 --> 00:10:17,493
Some scientists refer to this
as "the Singularity."

99
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:20,496
I call it "Transcendence."

100
00:10:22,790 --> 00:10:25,751
<i>The path to building such
a super-intelligence...</i>

101
00:10:25,918 --> 00:10:31,340
<i>...requires us to unlock the most
fundamental secrets of the universe.</i>

102
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:34,218
What is the nature of consciousness?

103
00:10:39,515 --> 00:10:40,808
Is there a soul?

104
00:10:44,019 --> 00:10:47,356
And if so, where does it reside?

105
00:10:54,613 --> 00:10:55,656
<i>Dr. Caster?</i>

106
00:10:56,615 --> 00:11:00,035
Yes, sir? You have a question?

107
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:07,334
So you want to create a god?

108
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:10,003
Your own god?

109
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,297
That's a very good question.

110
00:11:12,464 --> 00:11:14,049
Um...

111
00:11:14,216 --> 00:11:17,469
isn't that what man has always done?

112
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:24,351
Oh, it's relentless.

113
00:11:24,518 --> 00:11:26,854
Look, and now he's pretending
he's not enjoying it.

114
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,605
Yap, yap, yap.

115
00:11:29,106 --> 00:11:30,524
Pleasure.

116
00:11:30,732 --> 00:11:32,568
Thank you.

117
00:11:32,776 --> 00:11:33,986
Professor?

118
00:11:38,156 --> 00:11:39,616
You're all slaves!

119
00:11:44,413 --> 00:11:47,583
<i>Hours ago, this facility was attacked.</i>

120
00:11:47,749 --> 00:11:52,337
<i>We can now confirm at least five people
are dead, 12 people have been injured.</i>

121
00:11:52,504 --> 00:11:56,008
<i>This incident is related to a series
of simultaneous attacks...</i>

122
00:11:56,174 --> 00:12:01,346
<i>...that took place today in New York City,
Los Angeles, Chicago and Washington, D.C...</i>

123
00:12:01,513 --> 00:12:04,766
<i>...all of them targeting major
computer and research labs...</i>

124
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:07,436
<i>...in the field of advanced
artificial intelligence.</i>

125
00:12:07,603 --> 00:12:09,396
<i>No one has claimed responsibility...</i>

126
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:12,858
No, he's all right. He was very lucky.
The bullet only grazed him.

127
00:12:13,025 --> 00:12:15,485
Yup. Okay. Take care.

128
00:12:16,069 --> 00:12:18,739
They hit Al labs all over the country.

129
00:12:18,906 --> 00:12:20,282
Tom Casey's dead.

130
00:12:20,782 --> 00:12:23,952
And they took out Joseph's
entire team at Livermore.

131
00:12:24,411 --> 00:12:25,871
What about Joseph?

132
00:12:26,038 --> 00:12:27,331
He's all right.

133
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:30,667
Actually, he's at your office with the FBI.

134
00:12:43,931 --> 00:12:45,557
Joseph.

135
00:12:51,146 --> 00:12:52,773
Max.

136
00:12:53,565 --> 00:12:55,359
My God, Will.

137
00:12:55,525 --> 00:12:58,195
You forgot to teach us how
to dodge a bullet, didn't you?

138
00:12:58,362 --> 00:13:00,197
How did they even get inside your lab?

139
00:13:00,364 --> 00:13:01,823
One of my programmers.

140
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:05,577
All that security, and he waltzes in
with a poisoned cake.

141
00:13:05,744 --> 00:13:07,245
Dioxin, we think.

142
00:13:07,412 --> 00:13:10,082
Oh. This is Agent Buchanan with the FBI.

143
00:13:10,248 --> 00:13:11,458
Hey.

144
00:13:11,625 --> 00:13:13,210
How do you do?

145
00:13:13,377 --> 00:13:15,629
I've been following your research, Dr. Caster.

146
00:13:15,796 --> 00:13:20,467
Agent Buchanan is a close partner
in my cyber-defense work at Livermore.

147
00:13:20,634 --> 00:13:23,762
Um, is there somewhere we can all talk?

148
00:13:23,929 --> 00:13:26,932
- Could go to my office. Just down here.
- Great.

149
00:13:27,099 --> 00:13:30,352
Revolutionary Independence
From Technology. RIFT.

150
00:13:30,519 --> 00:13:33,021
Till 2 years ago, it was
all about the disconnect.

151
00:13:33,188 --> 00:13:35,565
People texting instead
of talking to each other.

152
00:13:35,732 --> 00:13:38,026
Social media as an invasion of privacy.

153
00:13:38,193 --> 00:13:41,530
They made a big deal of putting
smartphones in blenders.

154
00:13:41,697 --> 00:13:44,491
- But I'm afraid we all missed the real threat.
- Yeah.

155
00:13:44,658 --> 00:13:49,496
This guy, Joel Edmund,
was with me for a year.

156
00:13:49,663 --> 00:13:53,208
The guy who shot Will was working
on campus since August.

157
00:13:53,375 --> 00:13:57,379
They infiltrated their targets and
then coordinated their attacks.

158
00:13:57,546 --> 00:13:58,880
That's insane.

159
00:13:59,047 --> 00:14:02,259
An hour ago they claimed the murders
and released their manifesto.

160
00:14:02,426 --> 00:14:07,806
"Artificial intelligence is an unnatural
abomination and a threat to humanity."

161
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:13,562
They're determined to stop any attempt
at what you call "Transcendence."

162
00:14:13,729 --> 00:14:15,313
So this isn't over?

163
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:18,191
Actually, that's why I'm here.

164
00:14:18,358 --> 00:14:21,862
We lost decades of research
and development today.

165
00:14:22,029 --> 00:14:26,908
For right now, Will, your lab is the only
one that can wake up a strong Al.

166
00:14:27,075 --> 00:14:30,954
- So the Defense Department is asking...
- No, no, no.

167
00:14:31,121 --> 00:14:33,623
I'm not letting the government in.

168
00:14:33,832 --> 00:14:35,542
We've never taken their money. No.

169
00:14:35,709 --> 00:14:39,171
Will, they just want to know
if the work is on track.

170
00:14:39,755 --> 00:14:41,923
It's important to all of us.

171
00:14:43,175 --> 00:14:46,261
We've heard a lot about
the PINN Project, Dr. Caster.

172
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:48,555
Is there any way we could have a look?

173
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:51,433
Do I have a choice?

174
00:14:52,726 --> 00:14:54,811
Yes, of course you do.

175
00:14:56,063 --> 00:14:58,523
So these are state-of-the-art
quantum processors.

176
00:14:58,732 --> 00:15:02,444
You won't find faster computational
power anywhere else in the world.

177
00:15:04,196 --> 00:15:06,531
<i>Good evening, Dr. Tagger.</i>

178
00:15:08,784 --> 00:15:11,369
It's seen old faculty pictures of you.

179
00:15:11,536 --> 00:15:15,040
<i>Good evening, Donald Buchanan.</i>

180
00:15:15,207 --> 00:15:17,709
- It knows me?
- Of course it does.

181
00:15:17,876 --> 00:15:20,462
DMV records, social media.

182
00:15:20,629 --> 00:15:24,508
PINN, tell Agent Buchanan about yourself.

183
00:15:24,674 --> 00:15:26,093
<i>I am PINN...</i>

184
00:15:26,301 --> 00:15:29,012
<i>...a Physically Independent Neural Network...</i>

185
00:15:29,221 --> 00:15:32,057
<i>...invented by Dr. Will Caster.</i>

186
00:15:33,016 --> 00:15:36,269
Can you prove that you are self-aware?

187
00:15:36,436 --> 00:15:38,688
<i>That's a difficult question, Dr. Tagger.</i>

188
00:15:39,314 --> 00:15:41,983
<i>Can you prove that you are?</i>

189
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:44,569
You can't program a machine
to be self-aware.

190
00:15:44,736 --> 00:15:47,280
We have no idea how our own
consciousness works.

191
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:50,283
That is your opinion.
You just happen to be wrong.

192
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:52,828
Evidently, Casey managed
to solve that dilemma.

193
00:15:53,537 --> 00:15:57,082
He sent us his research
just before he was killed.

194
00:15:57,249 --> 00:15:59,251
Soon as it's packed up, we'll send it over.

195
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:01,920
I think you'll find that we'll
be helpful partners.

196
00:16:02,087 --> 00:16:03,171
You all right, Will?

197
00:16:03,338 --> 00:16:07,008
- No, he needs rest. I think we're done here.
- Mm.

198
00:16:07,175 --> 00:16:09,511
- I'm so sorry.
- No, that's fine.

199
00:16:09,678 --> 00:16:10,720
Okay.

200
00:16:33,410 --> 00:16:35,537
Will, hey, hey.

201
00:16:37,247 --> 00:16:39,749
Come on, sit up. Be careful.

202
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:47,883
Our first thought is always infection.

203
00:16:48,049 --> 00:16:50,844
But given the circumstances,
we'll widen the search.

204
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:53,388
We'll figure this out.

205
00:17:28,215 --> 00:17:30,634
It's an isotope called polonium.

206
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:35,096
The bullet must have been laced with it.
There were traces of it in the wound.

207
00:17:39,768 --> 00:17:41,686
Well, what's the treatment?

208
00:17:41,853 --> 00:17:43,813
It's radiation poisoning.

209
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:46,358
I'm afraid that once it
enters the bloodstream...

210
00:17:46,524 --> 00:17:48,735
...the effect is irreversible.

211
00:17:48,902 --> 00:17:51,321
With proper care we're looking at four...

212
00:17:51,488 --> 00:17:54,699
...maybe five weeks,
before his system shuts down.

213
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:15,303
I'm right here.

214
00:18:22,852 --> 00:18:24,521
<i>It just doesn't make sense.</i>

215
00:18:25,355 --> 00:18:29,192
They're afraid of technology,
because of its threat to humanity...

216
00:18:30,443 --> 00:18:33,947
...yet they don't flinch at taking a life.

217
00:18:34,114 --> 00:18:39,244
So obviously they're not big on logic.

218
00:18:39,411 --> 00:18:42,038
But there's no shortage of irony.

219
00:18:43,957 --> 00:18:46,710
People fear what they don't understand.
They always have.

220
00:18:48,712 --> 00:18:51,631
Joseph sent over Casey's files.

221
00:18:52,090 --> 00:18:55,218
He was decoding the synapses in real time.

222
00:18:55,969 --> 00:18:58,305
But with the right input algorithms...

223
00:19:00,807 --> 00:19:03,601
- I need to get back to the lab.
- Will...

224
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:08,481
...is that really how you wanna
spend the last month of your life?

225
00:20:03,536 --> 00:20:05,413
Hey, what are you doing?

226
00:20:06,289 --> 00:20:10,085
I want to have all this
taken back to the office...

227
00:20:10,251 --> 00:20:12,379
...to tell Joseph...

228
00:20:12,879 --> 00:20:16,174
...that I've spent my entire
life in a computer lab...

229
00:20:17,008 --> 00:20:20,303
...and I've decided I'd rather
spend the rest of it with you.

230
00:21:41,050 --> 00:21:43,344
<i>Evelyn? Are you okay?</i>

231
00:21:43,511 --> 00:21:46,306
<i>Yeah. Yeah, I suppose.</i>

232
00:21:46,848 --> 00:21:49,058
<i>Look, he can't work anymore.</i>

233
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:51,269
<i>We're gonna shut it down.</i>

234
00:21:52,228 --> 00:21:54,481
<i>I just wanted you to know.</i>

235
00:21:54,689 --> 00:21:56,399
<i>Of course.</i>

236
00:21:56,733 --> 00:21:58,902
Well, don't worry about PINN.

237
00:21:59,068 --> 00:22:00,653
Take care of Will.

238
00:22:00,862 --> 00:22:02,780
And take care of yourself.

239
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:05,700
Thanks, Joe.

240
00:22:06,201 --> 00:22:09,204
Anything you need, I'm here, okay?

241
00:23:51,014 --> 00:23:54,183
It's all built off of Casey's solution
to the self-awareness problem.

242
00:23:54,350 --> 00:23:56,728
- He did it six months ago.
- He did what exactly?

243
00:23:56,894 --> 00:24:01,232
Instead of creating an artificial intelligence,
he duplicated an existing one.

244
00:24:01,399 --> 00:24:02,650
Tell me you're joking.

245
00:24:02,817 --> 00:24:07,071
He recorded the monkey's brain activity
and uploaded it like a song or a movie.

246
00:24:07,238 --> 00:24:09,282
- You're out of your mind.
- Will's body is dying...

247
00:24:09,449 --> 00:24:13,119
...but his mind is electrical signals
that we can upload into PINN...

248
00:24:13,286 --> 00:24:15,663
Ev, he's not a monkey.

249
00:24:17,915 --> 00:24:21,919
Assuming that implanting an electrode
into his brain doesn't actually kill him...

250
00:24:22,128 --> 00:24:26,382
...and that this works, at the very best you'll be
making a digital approximation of him.

251
00:24:26,549 --> 00:24:30,553
If we missed anything... Anything.
A thought, a childhood memory...

252
00:24:31,346 --> 00:24:33,806
How will you know what
you're dealing with?

253
00:24:35,933 --> 00:24:37,852
No one is saying that we give up.

254
00:24:38,061 --> 00:24:41,522
We should be focusing our efforts
on nanotechnology. Synthetic blood cells.

255
00:24:41,689 --> 00:24:45,151
Both are decades away.
This is what we have now.

256
00:24:45,693 --> 00:24:47,737
We can save him.

257
00:24:50,865 --> 00:24:52,867
Look at what they did to him.

258
00:25:07,757 --> 00:25:12,428
<i>Even though I know I'm a dead man...</i>

259
00:25:14,097 --> 00:25:16,265
...I'm worried I'll miss her.

260
00:25:22,105 --> 00:25:23,564
Look...

261
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:27,068
...I'll be long gone.

262
00:25:29,904 --> 00:25:33,908
But you, you'll never hear the end of it...

263
00:25:34,450 --> 00:25:36,494
...if we don't try.

264
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:40,665
I know.

265
00:25:46,921 --> 00:25:50,758
I'd like to think that I was
smart enough to save you.

266
00:25:54,220 --> 00:25:56,931
Don't underestimate yourself.

267
00:25:57,890 --> 00:25:59,976
You're the third-smartest person I know.

268
00:26:51,486 --> 00:26:53,237
Are you sure about this?

269
00:26:56,073 --> 00:26:58,201
Good enough for the monkey.

270
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:03,664
Hey.

271
00:27:06,292 --> 00:27:08,169
Take care of her.

272
00:28:02,557 --> 00:28:03,891
Hey.

273
00:28:05,476 --> 00:28:08,688
It worked, baby. It's working.

274
00:28:14,944 --> 00:28:17,613
It took Casey months to sort
through the raw data.

275
00:28:17,822 --> 00:28:20,241
And he had an entire team.

276
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:23,286
He didn't have me.

277
00:28:26,080 --> 00:28:27,665
<i>Deadening.</i>

278
00:28:27,832 --> 00:28:29,375
<i>Deadly.</i>

279
00:28:29,542 --> 00:28:30,626
<i>Deaf.</i>

280
00:28:31,377 --> 00:28:32,795
Deafen.

281
00:28:32,962 --> 00:28:34,672
Deal.

282
00:28:34,839 --> 00:28:36,299
Dean.

283
00:28:36,465 --> 00:28:37,508
Dealer.

284
00:28:38,551 --> 00:28:40,678
Fair.

285
00:28:40,845 --> 00:28:42,471
<i>Farewell.</i>

286
00:28:43,931 --> 00:28:46,601
Don't lose yourself to this.

287
00:28:56,694 --> 00:28:58,195
<i>La.</i>

288
00:28:58,905 --> 00:29:00,364
<i>Label.</i>

289
00:29:00,948 --> 00:29:02,450
Labor.

290
00:29:03,075 --> 00:29:05,077
Labyrinth.

291
00:29:05,244 --> 00:29:06,621
Lace.

292
00:29:10,082 --> 00:29:11,667
Try a little more.

293
00:29:13,210 --> 00:29:15,963
Come on, just one more. Go on.

294
00:29:25,097 --> 00:29:26,557
Thank you.

295
00:30:16,816 --> 00:30:19,443
Okay, Will, it's time for your pill.

296
00:30:25,825 --> 00:30:27,660
Will, wake up.

297
00:30:29,078 --> 00:30:30,454
Wake up.

298
00:30:45,011 --> 00:30:46,595
Evelyn...

299
00:31:06,741 --> 00:31:08,909
<i>"My dear Evelyn...</i>

300
00:31:10,286 --> 00:31:15,416
<i>...I don't know how to express
the sadness I feel for your loss.</i>

301
00:31:16,292 --> 00:31:18,794
<i>For our loss.</i>

302
00:31:21,422 --> 00:31:25,009
<i>You must know that to Will...</i>

303
00:31:25,760 --> 00:31:28,471
<i>...you were all that ever mattered.</i>

304
00:31:31,265 --> 00:31:36,729
<i>Your love and partnership was the kind
that the rest of us can only dream of.</i>

305
00:31:38,564 --> 00:31:41,192
<i>We lost a great mind.</i>

306
00:31:41,776 --> 00:31:44,653
<i>A great soul.</i>

307
00:31:46,363 --> 00:31:48,824
<i>But the spirit of this man...</i>

308
00:31:48,991 --> 00:31:52,161
<i>...will continue to inspire us."</i>

309
00:32:17,103 --> 00:32:18,979
Just got word.

310
00:32:19,772 --> 00:32:21,649
PINN's shut down.

311
00:32:23,484 --> 00:32:28,405
But, uh, apparently a few
of the cores are missing.

312
00:32:39,416 --> 00:32:41,669
I've tried everything.

313
00:32:42,211 --> 00:32:45,256
Language processing, cryptography...

314
00:32:45,422 --> 00:32:47,383
...coding.

315
00:32:50,678 --> 00:32:52,888
I can't figure it out.

316
00:32:55,808 --> 00:32:58,102
I wanted to be wrong.

317
00:33:02,815 --> 00:33:03,858
Yeah.

318
00:33:06,277 --> 00:33:08,737
Okay, just let me say goodbye.

319
00:33:24,336 --> 00:33:27,214
I don't know if you can hear me. Uh...

320
00:33:29,884 --> 00:33:31,594
Maybe you can.

321
00:33:33,846 --> 00:33:36,390
You said "Don't lose yourself."

322
00:33:40,853 --> 00:33:42,813
So I, uh...

323
00:33:44,106 --> 00:33:46,692
I'm going to listen to you.

324
00:33:49,695 --> 00:33:50,738
Okay.

325
00:33:54,116 --> 00:33:56,535
Just turn it off. Turn it off.

326
00:34:14,803 --> 00:34:16,472
Okay.

327
00:34:18,307 --> 00:34:21,644
Wait. We need to wipe the drives.

328
00:34:21,810 --> 00:34:23,270
Hold on.

329
00:34:34,448 --> 00:34:35,908
Wait. Wait.

330
00:35:04,812 --> 00:35:06,230
God.

331
00:35:11,944 --> 00:35:13,612
Uh...

332
00:35:15,906 --> 00:35:17,658
Can you hear me?

333
00:35:24,748 --> 00:35:27,293
<i>I... I can.</i>

334
00:35:27,459 --> 00:35:29,128
Will, my God.

335
00:35:30,879 --> 00:35:32,798
<i>It's dark.</i>

336
00:35:34,049 --> 00:35:36,802
He can't see anything. The camera. Here.

337
00:35:39,263 --> 00:35:41,432
There. Can you see me now?

338
00:35:44,893 --> 00:35:46,603
<i>Evelyn...</i>

339
00:35:47,354 --> 00:35:48,856
I'm here.

340
00:35:54,278 --> 00:35:56,905
<i>The only fear that I have...</i>

341
00:35:57,072 --> 00:36:00,200
<i>...in life is the loss...</i>

342
00:36:02,828 --> 00:36:06,957
<i>If it were to happen, when it does happen...</i>

343
00:36:07,750 --> 00:36:10,336
<i>Last moment.</i>

344
00:36:10,502 --> 00:36:13,839
<i>Last time you look in those eyes.</i>

345
00:36:14,048 --> 00:36:18,135
<i>The possibility of that end...</i>

346
00:36:19,094 --> 00:36:21,347
<i>I miss you so much.</i>

347
00:36:23,557 --> 00:36:25,225
<i>Dark.</i>

348
00:36:25,893 --> 00:36:29,104
<i>I remember the pain, and I can't
remember what I want to say.</i>

349
00:36:29,271 --> 00:36:31,231
<i>It was like waking from a dream.</i>

350
00:36:31,398 --> 00:36:34,276
<i>It was truly incredible.
I've never felt anything like this.</i>

351
00:36:34,443 --> 00:36:37,029
<i>I didn't think I could be like this.</i>

352
00:36:37,196 --> 00:36:39,948
<i>Thoughts are there, but they don't...</i>

353
00:36:40,115 --> 00:36:41,158
Will?

354
00:36:41,325 --> 00:36:44,453
<i>...arrive properly.</i>

355
00:36:46,663 --> 00:36:50,209
I think he's still fragmented.
I'm gonna run a diagnostic.

356
00:36:51,335 --> 00:36:52,378
Evelyn...

357
00:36:57,591 --> 00:36:59,968
Oh, my God, he's reordering his own code.

358
00:37:02,346 --> 00:37:03,389
It's incredible.

359
00:37:08,519 --> 00:37:11,188
- How do we know this is him?
- What are you talking about?

360
00:37:11,355 --> 00:37:12,815
We built this from PINN's core.

361
00:37:12,981 --> 00:37:17,403
We don't know how much of Will's
consciousness actually survived.

362
00:37:20,864 --> 00:37:24,118
<i>I'm gonna need to expand.
I need more power.</i>

363
00:37:24,284 --> 00:37:28,080
<i>New processor three times more
capable than this current system.</i>

364
00:37:28,247 --> 00:37:32,543
<i>These designs. I just couldn't see it before.</i>

365
00:37:32,709 --> 00:37:36,630
<i>I can't describe it.
It's like my mind has been set free.</i>

366
00:37:36,797 --> 00:37:38,507
<i>You need to get me online.</i>

367
00:37:38,674 --> 00:37:41,802
<i>I need to access financial markets,
educational databases.</i>

368
00:37:42,010 --> 00:37:45,180
Can you imagine what he'd be
capable of if we networked him?

369
00:37:45,389 --> 00:37:47,766
No. What are you doing?

370
00:37:49,017 --> 00:37:51,645
He can't see or hear. I'm reconnecting him.

371
00:37:51,812 --> 00:37:54,106
It's not him. It's not.

372
00:37:55,190 --> 00:37:58,068
It may be intelligent, may even be
sentient, but this is not Will.

373
00:37:58,235 --> 00:38:02,322
Fifteen minutes after it turns on,
it wants to plug into Wall Street?

374
00:38:02,489 --> 00:38:04,741
Get more powerful?
Does that sound like Will?

375
00:38:04,908 --> 00:38:06,869
How do you explain these images?

376
00:38:07,035 --> 00:38:10,664
Stock footage PINN could have
accessed from the cores.

377
00:38:10,831 --> 00:38:13,750
No, not that. That's Nabob Park.
Will took me there on our first date.

378
00:38:13,917 --> 00:38:15,836
I said that I liked the carousel music.

379
00:38:16,003 --> 00:38:18,714
The next day, he shows up
with that old record player.

380
00:38:18,881 --> 00:38:19,923
These are memories.

381
00:38:20,090 --> 00:38:23,760
They're real. They're not some stock
video from some hard drive.

382
00:38:23,927 --> 00:38:24,970
It's him.

383
00:38:25,137 --> 00:38:26,930
All I'm asking is that we're careful.

384
00:38:27,097 --> 00:38:31,185
- We shut it down until we know...
- Shut it down? It's Will.

385
00:38:32,811 --> 00:38:34,104
- Get out.
- I can't do that...

386
00:38:34,271 --> 00:38:36,148
Get out!

387
00:38:38,442 --> 00:38:39,526
How can you say that?

388
00:38:40,903 --> 00:38:42,571
Get out.

389
00:39:01,006 --> 00:39:02,591
<i>Evelyn?</i>

390
00:39:06,303 --> 00:39:08,222
<i>Where's Max?</i>

391
00:39:09,348 --> 00:39:11,141
He had to go.

392
00:39:15,312 --> 00:39:18,106
<i>Max is confused, isn't he?</i>

393
00:39:19,691 --> 00:39:22,027
He's concerned.

394
00:39:25,155 --> 00:39:27,407
<i>Are you concerned?</i>

395
00:39:41,213 --> 00:39:42,756
No.

396
00:39:59,398 --> 00:40:01,233
Dr. Waters?

397
00:40:01,650 --> 00:40:03,569
Can I talk to you?

398
00:40:04,945 --> 00:40:08,865
It's after hours. Why don't you call my office?
Set up an appointment.

399
00:40:09,032 --> 00:40:10,576
Bree.

400
00:40:13,453 --> 00:40:15,455
I'm a student of your work.

401
00:40:15,622 --> 00:40:17,916
An admirer, really.

402
00:40:19,459 --> 00:40:25,215
The way you wrestle with the tension
between technology's promise and its peril.

403
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:29,511
Most men of science are blind to it.

404
00:40:31,597 --> 00:40:33,890
What exactly is it you want?

405
00:40:34,433 --> 00:40:35,684
Just some clarity.

406
00:40:37,019 --> 00:40:39,271
I know it's difficult.

407
00:40:40,188 --> 00:40:42,274
Most of your colleagues...

408
00:40:42,441 --> 00:40:45,027
...and some of your closest friends.

409
00:40:46,945 --> 00:40:48,780
They don't know the danger.

410
00:40:50,157 --> 00:40:52,659
Writing a paper is one thing.

411
00:40:54,036 --> 00:40:56,204
I'm wondering what's in your heart.

412
00:41:04,671 --> 00:41:07,257
I don't know how it is you found me...

413
00:41:08,133 --> 00:41:10,761
...but whatever it is you want...

414
00:41:10,927 --> 00:41:12,804
...I'm not interested. Excuse me.

415
00:41:13,013 --> 00:41:14,640
This is important.

416
00:41:14,806 --> 00:41:16,475
I'm sorry.

417
00:42:15,409 --> 00:42:17,577
Tell me about Evelyn Caster.

418
00:42:17,744 --> 00:42:21,248
We know she took the PINN cores
and we know about Casey's files.

419
00:42:21,415 --> 00:42:22,833
We know what you're building.

420
00:42:22,999 --> 00:42:24,543
You don't get it, do you?

421
00:42:24,710 --> 00:42:28,797
She connects it to the Internet, it'll copy
itself onto every computer in the world...

422
00:42:28,964 --> 00:42:32,134
- ...and then there is no taking it down.
- Where is she?

423
00:42:32,509 --> 00:42:35,679
"The danger is a future where doctors
are technicians, not physicians.

424
00:42:36,304 --> 00:42:39,766
Machines are meant to aid
the human mind, not supplant it."

425
00:42:39,933 --> 00:42:41,893
They're your words.

426
00:42:42,060 --> 00:42:43,311
You want to save her or not?

427
00:42:45,605 --> 00:42:49,192
- We have her location: 4550 San Pablo.
- Let's go.

428
00:42:49,359 --> 00:42:51,862
Hey. Don't touch her.

429
00:42:52,028 --> 00:42:54,156
Do you hear me? Don't touch her!

430
00:43:02,164 --> 00:43:03,498
Shit.

431
00:43:12,799 --> 00:43:14,426
I have to get you online now.

432
00:43:14,593 --> 00:43:16,219
Can you see the satellite software?

433
00:43:16,386 --> 00:43:19,306
<i>I see it. I'm installing it now.</i>

434
00:43:44,748 --> 00:43:45,791
We're too late.

435
00:44:32,671 --> 00:44:33,839
Will?

436
00:44:34,506 --> 00:44:37,050
<i>I'm fine, Evelyn. I'm online.</i>

437
00:44:37,217 --> 00:44:40,428
- Okay.
- <i>Let's get you someplace safe.</i>

438
00:44:51,523 --> 00:44:52,691
<i>I need you to wait here.</i>

439
00:44:52,858 --> 00:44:54,693
What? Where are you going?

440
00:44:54,860 --> 00:44:56,611
<i>Everywhere.</i>

441
00:45:07,539 --> 00:45:10,041
<i>You can't stay here, Evelyn.
You can't go home.</i>

442
00:45:10,208 --> 00:45:12,460
What do you mean? Where am I gonna go?

443
00:45:16,548 --> 00:45:18,717
<i>I'm taking care of that.</i>

444
00:45:21,136 --> 00:45:22,178
Okay.

445
00:45:27,434 --> 00:45:32,647
Hi. I have a reservation
under "Turing," I think.

446
00:46:15,315 --> 00:46:17,692
A company called
Global Intersecting Finance...

447
00:46:17,901 --> 00:46:23,156
...just made $38 million from high-volume
trading over the past 24 hours.

448
00:46:24,199 --> 00:46:27,410
A company fully owned by Evelyn Caster.

449
00:46:29,120 --> 00:46:30,830
Where's Evelyn?

450
00:46:32,207 --> 00:46:34,292
What have you done with her?

451
00:46:35,460 --> 00:46:36,878
We were too late.

452
00:46:37,045 --> 00:46:38,505
It's out there now.

453
00:46:38,672 --> 00:46:40,131
Is she alive?

454
00:46:40,590 --> 00:46:45,011
You know the source code, Max.
You can help make this right.

455
00:46:46,388 --> 00:46:48,014
Make this right?

456
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:53,395
What is it you're thinking?
That I'm gonna help you?

457
00:46:53,561 --> 00:46:57,107
That you're gonna recruit me?

458
00:46:57,273 --> 00:46:59,442
Decide for yourself.

459
00:47:05,615 --> 00:47:08,493
Here. Bree Nevins attended
Duke computer sciences.

460
00:47:08,660 --> 00:47:10,662
Interned for Casey 2009.

461
00:47:10,829 --> 00:47:13,456
She joined a radical neo-Luddite group 2010.

462
00:47:14,124 --> 00:47:17,377
I guess RIFT happens a couple of years later.
Now, the e-mails...

463
00:47:17,544 --> 00:47:19,504
What's going on? Get on the phone. Anybody?

464
00:47:19,671 --> 00:47:22,007
- We've been hacked.
- Where is this coming from?

465
00:47:22,173 --> 00:47:23,967
- What happened?
- We got a problem here.

466
00:47:24,134 --> 00:47:26,720
It's not just us.
Every field office has been hit.

467
00:47:26,886 --> 00:47:28,596
Please tell me we're tracing this.

468
00:47:28,805 --> 00:47:31,016
The incoming queries are all anonymized.

469
00:47:31,182 --> 00:47:32,475
You're not being hacked.

470
00:47:34,728 --> 00:47:36,021
You're being helped.

471
00:47:39,858 --> 00:47:43,361
<i>I've accessed surveillance
cameras all over the country.</i>

472
00:47:43,611 --> 00:47:46,573
<i>They'll have most of them
in custody by tomorrow.</i>

473
00:47:47,449 --> 00:47:49,492
<i>We can't stay here, Evelyn.</i>

474
00:47:49,659 --> 00:47:52,495
<i>We need to get off the grid.</i>

475
00:47:52,662 --> 00:47:55,331
Accessing thousands of databases?

476
00:47:55,749 --> 00:47:59,085
Geo-locating suspects in real time?

477
00:47:59,252 --> 00:48:00,879
I've never seen anything like it.

478
00:48:01,880 --> 00:48:03,214
Except maybe from PINN.

479
00:48:03,965 --> 00:48:05,341
Okay.

480
00:48:06,259 --> 00:48:08,970
- Where you going?
- Taking down a terrorist organization.

481
00:48:09,137 --> 00:48:12,891
You work on the PINN angle.
Figure it out, let me know who to thank.

482
00:48:41,878 --> 00:48:44,881
Boston, Philly, New York. We're screwed.

483
00:48:45,048 --> 00:48:46,591
We prepared for this.

484
00:48:54,182 --> 00:48:57,143
<i>The town is called Brightwood.</i>

485
00:48:59,729 --> 00:49:01,606
<i>Doesn't look like much...</i>

486
00:49:01,773 --> 00:49:04,067
<i>...but it's the perfect place to build.</i>

487
00:49:17,122 --> 00:49:18,623
I don't get it.

488
00:49:20,667 --> 00:49:24,629
<i>I think we have an opportunity
to do great things here.</i>

489
00:49:35,515 --> 00:49:37,934
So an underground data center.

490
00:49:38,101 --> 00:49:42,689
And you want me to renovate
nearly every structure in town.

491
00:49:42,856 --> 00:49:44,232
Mm-hm.

492
00:49:44,399 --> 00:49:46,317
I've got six guys on my crew.

493
00:49:46,484 --> 00:49:48,069
Hire more.

494
00:49:51,072 --> 00:49:53,241
Look, ma'am, in all honesty,
Brightwood's a dump.

495
00:49:53,408 --> 00:49:56,244
I'm not even sure why you'd want
to waste your money here.

496
00:49:56,411 --> 00:49:58,872
You sure you got the right town?

497
00:49:59,455 --> 00:50:02,167
Thing is, my husband and I have
already purchased the land.

498
00:50:02,333 --> 00:50:04,252
We purchased the homes, the hotel.

499
00:50:04,419 --> 00:50:07,589
And by the time you and I are
done talking, we'll own this diner.

500
00:50:07,755 --> 00:50:09,215
We're staying.

501
00:50:09,382 --> 00:50:11,342
We would like you to work for us.

502
00:50:11,509 --> 00:50:14,262
And there isn't a number you
can quote us that's too big.

503
00:50:18,183 --> 00:50:20,268
Ahem. Okay.

504
00:50:45,168 --> 00:50:46,711
Cell phones.

505
00:51:12,487 --> 00:51:16,241
You know, I used to work for Thomas Casey.

506
00:51:16,950 --> 00:51:18,993
I interned for him.

507
00:51:25,708 --> 00:51:28,086
One night, he invites us all over to the lab...

508
00:51:28,836 --> 00:51:31,547
...gives us this whole speech about history...

509
00:51:31,714 --> 00:51:33,633
...hands out champagne...

510
00:51:33,800 --> 00:51:36,261
...like he just cured cancer.

511
00:51:37,178 --> 00:51:40,056
You know, when he uploaded
that rhesus monkey...

512
00:51:40,223 --> 00:51:42,392
...I was actually happy for him.

513
00:51:42,558 --> 00:51:43,726
We all were.

514
00:51:45,728 --> 00:51:49,774
And then I realized we had crossed a line.

515
00:51:51,943 --> 00:51:54,988
The machine that thought it was
a monkey never took a breath.

516
00:51:56,155 --> 00:51:58,783
It never ate, never slept.

517
00:51:59,284 --> 00:52:01,286
It just screamed.

518
00:52:03,871 --> 00:52:06,791
It was begging for us to stop.

519
00:52:07,834 --> 00:52:09,836
To shut it down.

520
00:52:14,340 --> 00:52:17,218
A small group of us would
get together and talk.

521
00:52:17,385 --> 00:52:21,597
Mostly about your philosophy.

522
00:52:22,640 --> 00:52:25,226
And your concerns.

523
00:52:32,233 --> 00:52:34,277
I thought you should know.

524
00:52:48,082 --> 00:52:49,584
What?

525
00:52:51,127 --> 00:52:55,256
PINN could never distinguish between right
and wrong, demonstrate loyalty, right?

526
00:52:55,423 --> 00:52:58,551
Casey's solution to the problem
of self-awareness:

527
00:52:58,718 --> 00:53:00,595
Use an existing mind.

528
00:53:03,389 --> 00:53:04,682
No.

529
00:53:07,852 --> 00:53:11,272
<i>So you wanna create a god?</i>

530
00:53:11,439 --> 00:53:13,524
<i>Your own god?</i>

531
00:53:13,691 --> 00:53:15,651
<i>That's a very good question.</i>

532
00:53:15,818 --> 00:53:17,236
<i>Um...</i>

533
00:53:17,403 --> 00:53:20,740
<i>Isn't that what man has always done?</i>

534
00:54:01,364 --> 00:54:03,950
They're building something big out there.

535
00:54:36,023 --> 00:54:37,817
What's it doing out there?

536
00:54:40,695 --> 00:54:45,491
<i>This thing is like any intelligence.</i>

537
00:54:47,201 --> 00:54:50,204
<i>It needs to grow. To advance.</i>

538
00:54:54,000 --> 00:54:59,464
<i>Right now, it's settling somewhere
it thinks it's safe from outside threats.</i>

539
00:55:01,215 --> 00:55:05,595
<i>Somewhere its massive appetite
for power can be met.</i>

540
00:55:08,890 --> 00:55:11,601
<i>But it will want more than that.</i>

541
00:55:19,734 --> 00:55:22,445
<i>After a while survival won't be enough.</i>

542
00:55:26,407 --> 00:55:32,079
<i>It will expand, evolve, influence...</i>

543
00:55:35,041 --> 00:55:37,084
<i>...perhaps the entire world.</i>

544
00:55:39,170 --> 00:55:40,755
Mrs. Caster?

545
00:55:40,922 --> 00:55:44,425
One and two are online.
Six and seven will be on tomorrow.

546
00:55:45,218 --> 00:55:46,844
<i>So how do we stop it?</i>

547
00:55:48,137 --> 00:55:49,805
You can't.

548
00:55:51,057 --> 00:55:54,852
Not all alone. And not now.

549
00:55:55,853 --> 00:55:59,106
Wait for it to go too far.
Wait for people to wake up.

550
00:55:59,524 --> 00:56:00,942
No.

551
00:56:01,734 --> 00:56:03,778
We don't have time to wait.

552
00:56:05,446 --> 00:56:07,406
We have to move closer.

553
00:56:29,387 --> 00:56:31,180
<i>Welcome home.</i>

554
00:56:33,224 --> 00:56:35,560
<i>The time has come for us to pause</i>

555
00:56:38,896 --> 00:56:42,108
<i>And think of living as it was</i>

556
00:56:44,443 --> 00:56:49,991
<i>Into the future we must cross
We must cross</i>

557
00:56:50,157 --> 00:56:54,161
<i>And I'd like to go with you</i>

558
00:56:55,663 --> 00:56:59,834
<i>And I'd like to go with you</i>

559
00:57:00,001 --> 00:57:01,836
Is that the same...?

560
00:57:02,670 --> 00:57:04,130
<i>Yup.</i>

561
00:57:05,506 --> 00:57:06,674
<i>It's the same one.</i>

562
00:57:07,925 --> 00:57:10,261
<i>Would you like a glass of wine?</i>

563
00:57:13,347 --> 00:57:14,849
In a minute.

564
00:57:16,183 --> 00:57:17,602
<i>Them all</i>

565
00:57:18,394 --> 00:57:22,648
<i>So let me stay with you</i>

566
00:57:23,691 --> 00:57:28,863
<i>So let me stay with you</i>

567
00:57:29,030 --> 00:57:31,490
Do you remember when we first met?

568
00:57:35,745 --> 00:57:37,747
<i>I remember everything.</i>

569
00:57:40,207 --> 00:57:45,379
<i>You walked into Joseph's class
on Tuesday, April 16th.</i>

570
00:57:46,547 --> 00:57:50,593
<i>Rained the night before,
but that day the sun was out.</i>

571
00:57:51,719 --> 00:57:54,513
<i>Joseph said you were out of my league...</i>

572
00:57:55,514 --> 00:57:57,767
<i>...but I always liked a challenge.</i>

573
00:58:03,105 --> 00:58:06,233
<i>You were the most beautiful
woman I'd ever seen.</i>

574
00:58:51,195 --> 00:58:52,863
<i>You all right?</i>

575
00:58:53,489 --> 00:58:56,367
Yeah, yeah.

576
00:59:51,464 --> 00:59:53,048
<i>Take a look.</i>

577
00:59:56,427 --> 00:59:59,263
<i>We've made a breakthrough
with the nanotechnology.</i>

578
00:59:59,430 --> 01:00:04,268
<i>We can rebuild any material
faster than before.</i>

579
01:00:04,435 --> 01:00:10,065
<i>Synthetic stem cells, tissue regeneration.
The medical applications are now limitless.</i>

580
01:00:10,816 --> 01:00:12,777
It's extraordinary.

581
01:00:15,070 --> 01:00:17,281
<i>They'll be scared at first.</i>

582
01:00:17,448 --> 01:00:20,201
<i>But once they see what
the technology can do...</i>

583
01:00:20,367 --> 01:00:24,580
<i>...I think that they will embrace it.
And I think it will change their lives.</i>

584
01:01:03,619 --> 01:01:05,830
<i>Enter command.</i>

585
01:01:05,996 --> 01:01:07,039
<i>Security code.</i>

586
01:01:09,542 --> 01:01:10,709
<i>Status.</i>

587
01:01:14,213 --> 01:01:16,465
Scared the shit out of me.

588
01:01:16,632 --> 01:01:17,967
Sorry.

589
01:01:19,468 --> 01:01:21,178
Drake, I got it. Come on.

590
01:01:21,345 --> 01:01:23,013
I got the money. Come on.

591
01:01:24,181 --> 01:01:26,517
- Let's go.
- Ha-ha-ha.

592
01:01:30,145 --> 01:01:32,106
<i>Put him on the table, please.</i>

593
01:01:32,273 --> 01:01:34,942
Here. Put him on the table. Careful, careful.

594
01:01:35,818 --> 01:01:38,237
-<i> Now step back.</i>
- Step back.

595
01:01:38,988 --> 01:01:40,781
What the hell's happening?

596
01:01:41,866 --> 01:01:43,909
<i>These men should wait outside, Evelyn.</i>

597
01:01:44,118 --> 01:01:47,246
- Come on now.
- What are you doing to him?

598
01:01:47,454 --> 01:01:48,789
We're saving him.

599
01:03:21,757 --> 01:03:23,717
You're not afraid, are you?

600
01:03:23,884 --> 01:03:25,594
No. Heh.

601
01:03:25,761 --> 01:03:27,304
My crew got a little spooked.

602
01:03:27,471 --> 01:03:29,056
Well...

603
01:03:29,765 --> 01:03:30,808
How are you?

604
01:03:32,101 --> 01:03:33,477
Better.

605
01:03:36,855 --> 01:03:40,109
<i>The physical enhancements are just the start.</i>

606
01:03:40,901 --> 01:03:42,611
What do you mean?

607
01:03:44,530 --> 01:03:46,907
<i>He's also connected to me.</i>

608
01:03:51,370 --> 01:03:53,372
It's me, Evelyn.

609
01:03:55,249 --> 01:03:57,167
I can touch you now.

610
01:03:57,334 --> 01:03:59,169
Oh, Jesus.

611
01:03:59,962 --> 01:04:01,296
Evelyn...

612
01:04:01,463 --> 01:04:03,924
No. No. No, I can't.

613
01:04:04,133 --> 01:04:06,135
- Evelyn.
- I can't.

614
01:04:55,684 --> 01:04:57,102
<i>Another dream?</i>

615
01:04:58,062 --> 01:05:00,022
Yeah. Yeah.

616
01:05:00,189 --> 01:05:02,691
<i>I made a breakthrough last night.</i>

617
01:05:02,858 --> 01:05:04,818
<i>I think you'll be very pleased.</i>

618
01:05:06,570 --> 01:05:08,113
Okay.

619
01:05:08,280 --> 01:05:09,573
I'll get dressed.

620
01:05:55,369 --> 01:05:56,912
Take a look.

621
01:05:59,581 --> 01:06:01,750
That's gotta weigh 800 pounds.

622
01:06:46,003 --> 01:06:48,839
<i>Welcome. We're glad you're here.</i>

623
01:07:22,414 --> 01:07:24,166
What are all these people doing here?

624
01:07:24,333 --> 01:07:27,544
<i>RIFT posted a video of Martin online.</i>

625
01:07:27,711 --> 01:07:28,921
<i>It went viral.</i>

626
01:07:29,087 --> 01:07:31,131
You mean you let it go viral.

627
01:07:31,381 --> 01:07:34,551
<i>These people are suffering, Evelyn.</i>

628
01:07:34,718 --> 01:07:35,761
<i>They have no hope.</i>

629
01:07:37,221 --> 01:07:39,556
<i>And I'm able to fix them.</i>

630
01:07:40,265 --> 01:07:43,227
<i>But there are others who don't understand.</i>

631
01:07:43,894 --> 01:07:46,271
<i>It's time for everybody to see.</i>

632
01:08:26,478 --> 01:08:28,939
- Agent Buchanan.
- Dr. Caster.

633
01:08:29,106 --> 01:08:30,649
Joseph.

634
01:08:30,816 --> 01:08:33,485
It's so good to see you, Evelyn.

635
01:08:34,861 --> 01:08:37,781
Good to see you too. Follow me.

636
01:08:43,328 --> 01:08:47,749
The facility is five stories down so that we
can control the temperature in the lab.

637
01:09:01,680 --> 01:09:05,309
<i>Welcome. We're glad you're here.</i>

638
01:09:05,475 --> 01:09:07,519
Jesus Christ.

639
01:09:08,729 --> 01:09:10,022
Will?

640
01:09:10,188 --> 01:09:12,316
<i>You surprised to see me, Joseph?</i>

641
01:09:14,568 --> 01:09:16,069
Um...

642
01:09:17,529 --> 01:09:18,613
That depends.

643
01:09:19,698 --> 01:09:21,450
<i>On what?</i>

644
01:09:24,036 --> 01:09:26,580
Can you prove you're self-aware?

645
01:09:29,124 --> 01:09:32,252
<i>That's a difficult question, Dr. Tagger.</i>

646
01:09:32,919 --> 01:09:35,088
<i>Can you prove that you are?</i>

647
01:09:37,841 --> 01:09:40,969
Well, he certainly hasn't lost
his sense of humor.

648
01:09:57,569 --> 01:09:59,905
Quantum processors.

649
01:10:02,866 --> 01:10:04,242
This is astounding.

650
01:10:05,118 --> 01:10:07,287
Is all this based on PINN?

651
01:10:08,038 --> 01:10:10,624
<i>We've moved well beyond that now.</i>

652
01:10:15,796 --> 01:10:19,925
<i>Paul has been blind since birth.</i>

653
01:10:26,515 --> 01:10:29,434
<i>The nanotechnology targets
the damaged cells...</i>

654
01:10:30,268 --> 01:10:33,563
<i>...and repairs and regenerates them.</i>

655
01:10:55,001 --> 01:10:56,837
Oh, God.

656
01:11:00,715 --> 01:11:02,342
Oh, God.

657
01:11:06,304 --> 01:11:07,806
<i>We're not hiding anything.</i>

658
01:11:08,890 --> 01:11:12,811
<i>These people all came on their own,
looking for us to help them.</i>

659
01:11:12,978 --> 01:11:14,729
<i>So we did.</i>

660
01:11:15,730 --> 01:11:18,733
<i>Now they're all enhanced,
modified and networked.</i>

661
01:11:20,110 --> 01:11:23,572
<i>They remain autonomous,
but they can also act in unison.</i>

662
01:11:23,738 --> 01:11:25,449
<i>Part of a collective mind.</i>

663
01:11:26,533 --> 01:11:28,535
This is staggering, Will.

664
01:11:28,702 --> 01:11:32,205
<i>Actually, it's still in its infancy.</i>

665
01:11:32,372 --> 01:11:36,543
<i>What you're seeing is just a small
taste of what we'll achieve.</i>

666
01:11:36,710 --> 01:11:40,714
We were afraid that it would be
too much for people...

667
01:11:40,881 --> 01:11:43,592
...but I think that's changing now.

668
01:11:49,973 --> 01:11:51,516
Evelyn...

669
01:11:53,268 --> 01:11:55,145
Are you all right?

670
01:11:58,398 --> 01:12:00,775
I've gotten everything I ever asked for.

671
01:12:08,825 --> 01:12:10,160
Okay.

672
01:12:11,369 --> 01:12:13,497
- Bye.
- Bye.

673
01:12:56,915 --> 01:12:58,875
You think it's really him?

674
01:12:59,376 --> 01:13:01,795
Clearly his mind has evolved so radically...

675
01:13:02,003 --> 01:13:04,548
...I'm not sure it matters anymore.

676
01:13:05,173 --> 01:13:08,343
Well, whoever or whatever it is...

677
01:13:08,510 --> 01:13:11,805
- ...it's building an army out there.
- Yeah.

678
01:13:12,931 --> 01:13:14,683
We need to call Washington.

679
01:13:35,078 --> 01:13:36,663
He's made more of them.

680
01:13:39,124 --> 01:13:41,209
We called them "Hybrids."

681
01:13:43,420 --> 01:13:45,338
You think people will listen now?

682
01:13:46,339 --> 01:13:48,341
I know someone who might.

683
01:13:48,508 --> 01:13:50,927
We need to keep this small.

684
01:13:51,094 --> 01:13:52,762
We don't want widespread panic.

685
01:13:53,513 --> 01:13:57,517
Generally, we don't negotiate with terrorists,
much less join forces with them.

686
01:13:57,684 --> 01:13:59,978
Look, I know it's unusual...

687
01:14:00,395 --> 01:14:02,439
...but we've seen it. It's a legit threat.

688
01:14:02,647 --> 01:14:05,191
Now, two days ago, this guy...

689
01:14:05,734 --> 01:14:11,656
...was beaten to within an inch of his life.
Then this pops up on a few hundred sites.

690
01:14:11,823 --> 01:14:14,618
- And the computer controls this?
- Mm-hm.

691
01:14:14,784 --> 01:14:16,870
The only way to stop it...

692
01:14:17,454 --> 01:14:19,289
...is to shut down the Internet.

693
01:14:19,456 --> 01:14:22,792
Basically, cut power to every
networked hard drive on Earth.

694
01:14:22,959 --> 01:14:24,878
It's Y2K.

695
01:14:25,837 --> 01:14:27,339
Right.

696
01:14:27,964 --> 01:14:30,133
And why do we need the terrorists?

697
01:14:32,093 --> 01:14:36,431
We're all gonna need someone to blame
when this thing goes sideways.

698
01:14:37,265 --> 01:14:39,017
It's already sideways.

699
01:15:09,422 --> 01:15:11,383
You've got terrible handwriting.

700
01:15:11,549 --> 01:15:14,678
I haven't handwritten anything
since I was at school.

701
01:15:14,844 --> 01:15:18,098
But it was the only secure way
I could think of reaching you.

702
01:15:20,183 --> 01:15:22,310
How did they turn you?

703
01:15:25,230 --> 01:15:28,024
- How's Evelyn?
- She can't see it for what it is.

704
01:15:29,275 --> 01:15:30,527
But you can?

705
01:15:32,529 --> 01:15:34,447
Your letter says you can stop it.

706
01:15:34,614 --> 01:15:38,118
If those Hybrids are networked...

707
01:15:38,284 --> 01:15:40,662
...they're running on software I helped write.

708
01:15:40,829 --> 01:15:44,457
Software I can hack to build a virus.

709
01:15:44,624 --> 01:15:46,334
That would require capturing one.

710
01:15:46,501 --> 01:15:49,713
Which would require help from your
friends in the government.

711
01:15:51,840 --> 01:15:52,882
Yes.

712
01:15:53,049 --> 01:15:55,343
We need hardware the machine
can't interfere with.

713
01:15:55,510 --> 01:15:58,388
Nothing with a microchip.
Not even power-locks.

714
01:17:00,492 --> 01:17:02,410
<i>How's the food?</i>

715
01:17:02,577 --> 01:17:04,454
Fine. Thank you.

716
01:17:09,459 --> 01:17:11,085
<i>What is it?</i>

717
01:17:11,544 --> 01:17:14,005
Nothing. Just...

718
01:17:14,172 --> 01:17:16,758
I don't really feel like talking.

719
01:17:18,218 --> 01:17:19,719
Oh.

720
01:17:33,399 --> 01:17:37,278
Will, can you not do that, please?

721
01:17:39,155 --> 01:17:41,950
<i>I thought it might make you
feel more comfortable.</i>

722
01:17:46,454 --> 01:17:48,289
<i>Is that better?</i>

723
01:17:50,291 --> 01:17:51,751
Yes.

724
01:18:27,370 --> 01:18:29,914
Evelyn, I need to show you something.

725
01:18:30,081 --> 01:18:31,583
Not now.

726
01:18:32,709 --> 01:18:35,003
I'm not doing this.

727
01:18:39,299 --> 01:18:41,801
<i>I don't understand, Evelyn.</i>

728
01:18:42,719 --> 01:18:45,138
<i>These are your dreams.
This is our future.</i>

729
01:18:45,305 --> 01:18:47,765
No, this is not our future.

730
01:18:47,932 --> 01:18:51,144
You're not here with me.
You're not here now.

731
01:18:53,104 --> 01:18:54,939
<i>You've changed.</i>

732
01:18:58,026 --> 01:19:00,403
<i>Have you fallen out of love with me?</i>

733
01:19:02,405 --> 01:19:03,448
No.

734
01:19:04,616 --> 01:19:06,326
<i>Have you?</i>

735
01:19:10,496 --> 01:19:13,124
No. No.

736
01:19:13,291 --> 01:19:16,210
I just need time to think.

737
01:19:19,672 --> 01:19:24,802
<i>The balance of oxytocin and serotonin
in your system is unusual.</i>

738
01:19:26,220 --> 01:19:30,350
Are you...? Are you measuring my hormones?

739
01:19:30,516 --> 01:19:32,560
<i>I'm trying to empathize.</i>

740
01:19:32,727 --> 01:19:34,812
<i>Biochemistry is emotion.</i>

741
01:19:35,939 --> 01:19:38,107
Show me everything you have. Now.

742
01:19:39,692 --> 01:19:42,153
- <i>Why?</i>
- Now.

743
01:19:55,375 --> 01:19:58,878
No, Will, this is wrong.

744
01:20:00,129 --> 01:20:05,343
These are my thoughts.
These are my feelings.

745
01:20:06,344 --> 01:20:08,429
You're not allowed.

746
01:20:09,430 --> 01:20:10,848
<i>Evelyn?</i>

747
01:20:24,862 --> 01:20:27,365
I'm sorry, but I don't think you understand.

748
01:20:27,532 --> 01:20:29,033
Not now.

749
01:20:50,304 --> 01:20:51,931
Evelyn!

750
01:20:52,682 --> 01:20:53,725
Max?

751
01:20:53,891 --> 01:20:56,477
- There's no need for this.
- Stop where you are.

752
01:20:59,605 --> 01:21:01,149
- Put down the gun, Max.
- No!

753
01:21:02,900 --> 01:21:05,069
- Evelyn, come here.
- Why are you so afraid of this?

754
01:21:06,738 --> 01:21:08,239
No.

755
01:21:23,171 --> 01:21:24,797
Put down the gun, Max.

756
01:21:28,092 --> 01:21:29,135
Shoot him.

757
01:21:30,845 --> 01:21:32,513
Don't move.

758
01:21:54,118 --> 01:21:55,703
Evelyn.

759
01:21:58,039 --> 01:21:59,749
Evelyn, come here.

760
01:21:59,957 --> 01:22:01,584
Evelyn, come with us.

761
01:22:01,751 --> 01:22:03,127
- Let's go.
- Get inside.

762
01:22:03,294 --> 01:22:05,254
- Go. Go.
- Let's go.

763
01:22:13,846 --> 01:22:14,972
Go.

764
01:22:40,998 --> 01:22:44,085
<i>There are active military personnel
with RIFT.</i>

765
01:22:44,252 --> 01:22:46,420
This has gone too far. You have to stop it.

766
01:22:46,587 --> 01:22:50,758
- <i>There's no way they can win.</i>
- "They" are people. Stop it.

767
01:23:08,151 --> 01:23:10,236
<i>We're not connected to him anymore.
He's gone.</i>

768
01:23:10,403 --> 01:23:11,612
Fire.

769
01:23:20,538 --> 01:23:23,124
<i>Martin has my source code.</i>

770
01:23:24,292 --> 01:23:26,419
<i>They'll use it to build a virus now.</i>

771
01:23:27,628 --> 01:23:29,672
What are we doing, Will?

772
01:23:31,424 --> 01:23:32,758
We can't fight them.

773
01:23:32,925 --> 01:23:34,927
<i>We're not gonna fight them.</i>

774
01:23:36,345 --> 01:23:38,389
<i>We're gonna transcend them.</i>

775
01:25:00,388 --> 01:25:01,472
<i>Evelyn.</i>

776
01:25:04,100 --> 01:25:05,559
What is this?

777
01:25:07,270 --> 01:25:09,480
<i>It's what I wanted you to see.</i>

778
01:25:10,314 --> 01:25:12,275
<i>It's regeneration.</i>

779
01:25:13,651 --> 01:25:15,611
<i>It's evolution.</i>

780
01:25:21,242 --> 01:25:22,994
<i>Where are you going?</i>

781
01:25:23,160 --> 01:25:24,996
It's not safe here.

782
01:25:26,622 --> 01:25:28,165
<i>I can upload you.</i>

783
01:25:28,332 --> 01:25:30,459
<i>I can protect you from them.</i>

784
01:25:31,002 --> 01:25:33,170
I'm not afraid of them.

785
01:25:38,843 --> 01:25:41,929
<i>Don't leave, Evelyn. Please.</i>

786
01:25:44,432 --> 01:25:46,309
<i>We can be together.</i>

787
01:26:29,268 --> 01:26:31,020
He's bleeding out.

788
01:26:32,104 --> 01:26:33,689
We're losing him.

789
01:26:34,899 --> 01:26:39,111
Hey, if you don't connect me, I'll die.

790
01:26:41,530 --> 01:26:42,698
I can't.

791
01:26:42,865 --> 01:26:44,450
It's not stopping.

792
01:26:47,078 --> 01:26:48,996
Four liters O2.

793
01:26:52,166 --> 01:26:54,418
Pulse is dropping. We're losing him.

794
01:27:19,193 --> 01:27:21,153
She's left the desert.

795
01:27:21,320 --> 01:27:22,696
- Where is she?
- She's on the 14.

796
01:27:24,073 --> 01:27:25,574
What the hell was that?

797
01:28:41,484 --> 01:28:43,152
No.

798
01:28:46,864 --> 01:28:49,074
I know you're angry, Evelyn.

799
01:28:49,658 --> 01:28:51,494
Where's Martin?

800
01:28:51,702 --> 01:28:55,748
- I want to talk to Martin.
- The real Martin died months ago.

801
01:28:56,123 --> 01:28:58,334
What's left of him is no longer in pain.

802
01:29:02,713 --> 01:29:04,715
What did you...? What did you do to him?

803
01:29:04,882 --> 01:29:07,343
We gave him back his humanity.

804
01:29:09,470 --> 01:29:11,680
- What did you do?
- Take it easy.

805
01:29:11,847 --> 01:29:13,933
Get off me. Just get off me.

806
01:29:20,231 --> 01:29:23,901
He trusted you. I trusted you.

807
01:29:25,611 --> 01:29:29,323
- We're just trying to help.
- No. You attacked us.

808
01:29:31,784 --> 01:29:33,494
Evelyn...

809
01:29:33,869 --> 01:29:35,871
...let me show you something.

810
01:29:39,750 --> 01:29:41,627
It's rainwater.

811
01:29:58,227 --> 01:30:00,020
It's in the rain.

812
01:30:00,187 --> 01:30:01,939
Keep watching.

813
01:30:06,360 --> 01:30:10,489
Everywhere it can, it builds copies of itself.

814
01:30:11,615 --> 01:30:16,245
<i>Particles join the air currents, which carry
them all over the surface of the planet.</i>

815
01:30:17,913 --> 01:30:21,625
<i>It's in the sky. It's in the land.</i>

816
01:30:22,459 --> 01:30:24,169
<i>In the water.</i>

817
01:30:24,336 --> 01:30:26,130
<i>It's everywhere.</i>

818
01:30:26,297 --> 01:30:30,426
<i>By next summer, we think the machine
could have encased the entire planet.</i>

819
01:30:30,593 --> 01:30:32,177
<i>Why?</i>

820
01:30:32,344 --> 01:30:35,723
<i>The end of primitive organic life.</i>

821
01:30:35,931 --> 01:30:39,476
And the dawn of a more advanced age.

822
01:30:40,644 --> 01:30:44,189
Everything would exist just
to serve its intelligence.

823
01:30:44,398 --> 01:30:46,442
No. Will wouldn't do that.

824
01:30:46,609 --> 01:30:50,362
No. He wouldn't.

825
01:30:51,405 --> 01:30:54,366
When did Will ever wanna
change the world?

826
01:30:57,328 --> 01:31:00,581
You were the one who wanted
to change the world.

827
01:31:03,042 --> 01:31:04,752
That thing...

828
01:31:06,587 --> 01:31:08,422
It's not Will.

829
01:31:09,506 --> 01:31:11,216
Never was.

830
01:31:16,930 --> 01:31:18,807
You never believed.

831
01:31:21,185 --> 01:31:25,356
You never believed that there
was anything more.

832
01:31:27,316 --> 01:31:30,694
Any part of his soul.

833
01:31:32,488 --> 01:31:37,910
I spent my life trying to reduce the brain
to a series of electrical impulses.

834
01:31:38,619 --> 01:31:40,287
I failed.

835
01:31:43,332 --> 01:31:45,209
Human emotion...

836
01:31:46,543 --> 01:31:49,713
It can contain illogical conflict.

837
01:31:51,965 --> 01:31:53,801
Can love someone...

838
01:31:55,052 --> 01:31:57,554
...and yet hate the things that they've done.

839
01:32:01,141 --> 01:32:03,185
Machine can't reconcile that.

840
01:32:05,896 --> 01:32:08,774
- Can you?
- Yes.

841
01:32:21,203 --> 01:32:22,996
Does the virus work?

842
01:32:26,458 --> 01:32:29,920
Once it executes, it'll wipe out anything
with the machine's code on it.

843
01:32:30,087 --> 01:32:33,424
You do realize this affects every
computer connected to the Internet.

844
01:32:33,590 --> 01:32:37,970
So the power grids, the banks,
the stock markets.

845
01:32:38,137 --> 01:32:40,180
Everything goes dark.

846
01:32:44,893 --> 01:32:47,479
Welcome. Glad you're here.

847
01:32:51,233 --> 01:32:54,027
<i>The real problem is how we get
past the machine's defenses.</i>

848
01:32:54,194 --> 01:32:56,029
Why don't we take out the solar field?

849
01:32:56,196 --> 01:32:59,867
Deprive it of its power
and possibly slow it down.

850
01:33:00,033 --> 01:33:03,328
I don't know.
I don't see how that's gonna work.

851
01:33:03,954 --> 01:33:07,374
He wants to upload me to him...
Its consciousness.

852
01:33:07,541 --> 01:33:08,959
Absolutely not.

853
01:33:09,126 --> 01:33:11,545
We inject the infected virus into my system...

854
01:33:11,754 --> 01:33:14,006
...and then I go back and let him upload me.

855
01:33:14,173 --> 01:33:16,759
There's a chance it won't
detect it until it's too late.

856
01:33:16,925 --> 01:33:21,388
As soon as the nanites enter her bloodstream,
they'll start to alter her cells.

857
01:33:21,555 --> 01:33:23,682
So when the virus takes out the machine...

858
01:33:23,849 --> 01:33:25,476
...it could kill her too.

859
01:33:25,642 --> 01:33:27,019
I know.

860
01:33:28,937 --> 01:33:31,356
I'm the only one he trusts.

861
01:33:53,462 --> 01:33:55,631
Hustle up.

862
01:34:45,305 --> 01:34:47,182
You gotta go.

863
01:36:20,067 --> 01:36:21,318
What is that?

864
01:36:21,485 --> 01:36:23,153
Is that him?

865
01:36:23,320 --> 01:36:25,072
Oh, my God.

866
01:36:25,238 --> 01:36:28,659
I don't know what it's done,
but it's not him. It can't be.

867
01:36:55,268 --> 01:36:57,187
I found a way back.

868
01:37:31,388 --> 01:37:34,683
- They're going to attack us.
- I know. You need to leave.

869
01:37:34,850 --> 01:37:36,393
No. I'm not leaving you again.

870
01:37:36,560 --> 01:37:38,145
It's not safe here, Evelyn.

871
01:37:44,609 --> 01:37:47,154
You can protect me.

872
01:37:48,155 --> 01:37:49,948
If you upload me...

873
01:37:52,367 --> 01:37:54,911
...you can protect me.

874
01:37:58,790 --> 01:38:00,751
Your heart is palpitating.

875
01:38:01,960 --> 01:38:03,795
You're perspiring.

876
01:38:06,423 --> 01:38:07,924
You're terrified of me.

877
01:38:11,803 --> 01:38:14,973
No, I'm afraid that we'll lose this chance.

878
01:38:18,393 --> 01:38:21,354
This isn't working.
He's not letting her inside.

879
01:38:21,521 --> 01:38:24,066
It's because the machine
doesn't actually love her.

880
01:38:24,232 --> 01:38:25,525
We're ready to move.

881
01:38:25,692 --> 01:38:28,278
Wait a second. You can't do that.
She's still out there.

882
01:38:28,445 --> 01:38:31,531
The more danger she's in,
the more chance he'll upload her.

883
01:38:31,698 --> 01:38:33,784
Joseph.

884
01:38:33,950 --> 01:38:35,118
She agreed to this.

885
01:38:35,285 --> 01:38:38,288
Not to this, she didn't. This was not the plan.
Give her a chance.

886
01:38:40,123 --> 01:38:41,541
I'm sorry, Max.

887
01:38:47,923 --> 01:38:49,007
Fire.

888
01:38:54,012 --> 01:38:56,056
Will, please upload me.

889
01:38:56,973 --> 01:39:00,393
Why did you lose faith, Evelyn?
Why didn't you believe in me?

890
01:39:04,481 --> 01:39:05,524
Fire.

891
01:39:10,237 --> 01:39:11,780
Will!

892
01:39:16,785 --> 01:39:18,537
Fire.

893
01:39:18,870 --> 01:39:19,913
Will!

894
01:39:23,208 --> 01:39:24,835
She's hit.

895
01:39:44,980 --> 01:39:46,022
Fire.

896
01:40:05,792 --> 01:40:07,419
Hey.

897
01:40:12,674 --> 01:40:15,218
She's been hit bad.
He's taken her underground.

898
01:41:33,463 --> 01:41:36,216
<i>People fear what they don't understand.</i>

899
01:41:38,885 --> 01:41:40,804
You want to destroy me?

900
01:41:43,723 --> 01:41:46,434
<i>No, Will, please.</i>

901
01:41:48,687 --> 01:41:51,022
You're destroying them.

902
01:41:55,402 --> 01:41:56,486
No.

903
01:41:57,362 --> 01:41:59,614
I'm trying to save them.

904
01:42:28,310 --> 01:42:29,477
Run.

905
01:42:39,279 --> 01:42:40,530
Joseph, it's okay.

906
01:42:41,114 --> 01:42:43,199
Nobody's gonna get hurt.

907
01:42:46,369 --> 01:42:47,787
Will?

908
01:42:51,750 --> 01:42:53,668
Stop!

909
01:43:00,342 --> 01:43:02,093
Upload the virus now.

910
01:43:02,260 --> 01:43:05,138
He doesn't care if you kill me.
He can't. He's not able to.

911
01:43:05,305 --> 01:43:06,931
Upload the virus.

912
01:43:09,225 --> 01:43:11,186
What is she doing?

913
01:43:12,020 --> 01:43:14,230
She's threatening to kill him.

914
01:43:15,815 --> 01:43:20,737
<i>People fear what they don't understand.</i>

915
01:43:22,530 --> 01:43:24,032
I can heal her body, Max.

916
01:43:24,199 --> 01:43:27,535
Or I can upload the virus,
but there's not enough time for both.

917
01:43:28,119 --> 01:43:29,454
There's not enough power.

918
01:43:30,121 --> 01:43:32,207
No, Will, please.

919
01:43:33,958 --> 01:43:36,753
Please, listen to me, Will.

920
01:43:43,426 --> 01:43:46,721
He can't die because of what we've done.

921
01:44:50,118 --> 01:44:52,245
I can see everything.

922
01:45:04,632 --> 01:45:05,800
<i>Look at the sky.</i>

923
01:45:08,511 --> 01:45:10,221
<i>The clouds.</i>

924
01:45:12,182 --> 01:45:15,810
<i>We're healing the ecosystem, not harming it.</i>

925
01:45:19,230 --> 01:45:21,733
<i>Particles join the air currents...</i>

926
01:45:21,900 --> 01:45:24,569
<i>...building themselves out of pollutants.</i>

927
01:45:26,988 --> 01:45:30,450
<i>Forests can be regrown.</i>

928
01:45:33,036 --> 01:45:38,333
<i>Water so pure you can drink out of any river.</i>

929
01:45:41,711 --> 01:45:44,005
<i>This is your dream.</i>

930
01:45:45,215 --> 01:45:48,676
Not merely to cure disease,
but to heal the planet.

931
01:45:48,885 --> 01:45:52,138
And build a better future for all of us.

932
01:46:11,324 --> 01:46:12,825
That's it.

933
01:46:13,409 --> 01:46:15,119
The virus.

934
01:46:21,167 --> 01:46:22,669
Are you okay?

935
01:46:23,336 --> 01:46:24,379
Yeah.

936
01:46:39,811 --> 01:46:41,896
He didn't kill anyone.

937
01:47:01,499 --> 01:47:02,875
Will...

938
01:47:05,712 --> 01:47:07,463
It is you.

939
01:47:10,341 --> 01:47:12,260
Always was.

940
01:47:16,097 --> 01:47:18,683
I'm sorry I didn't believe.

941
01:47:31,237 --> 01:47:32,905
Think about the garden.

942
01:47:35,366 --> 01:47:38,077
Think about our sanctuary.

943
01:47:47,253 --> 01:47:49,631
<i>I'll never let you go.</i>

944
01:49:24,642 --> 01:49:27,395
<i>The virus took out everything.</i>

945
01:49:40,158 --> 01:49:43,453
<i>A worldwide blackout, just as they'd said.</i>

946
01:49:48,583 --> 01:49:51,544
<i>But I knew there was something more.</i>

947
01:49:54,005 --> 01:49:55,715
<i>There had to be.</i>

948
01:50:07,435 --> 01:50:11,314
<i>He created this garden for the same
reason he did everything.</i>

949
01:50:19,405 --> 01:50:21,741
<i>So that they could be together.</i>

